@* FluentTabStrip (round wysiwyg-instruction-editor, owner 2026-10-11) — the repo's TRADITIONAL
   folder-tab chrome over FluentTabs, extracted for reuse: every tab wears a 1px border with rounded
   top corners; the PANEL carries one continuous top border across the full width; the SELECTED tab
   loses its bottom border and, filled opaque, masks the panel's line exactly beneath itself — the
   only break in that line — while unselected tabs keep theirs (coinciding with the panel's border,
   so it reads single). The v4 accent-underline suppression (an exposed ::part) has no v5
   equivalent — v5 keeps its indicator shadow-internal; see FluentTabStrip.razor.css.

   Pass FluentTab elements as children — FluentUI's semantics (aria-selected, keyboard navigation,
   and the hidden-panel behaviour rich editors inside tabs rely on) are preserved untouched:

       <FluentTabStrip>
           <FluentTab Header="First">…</FluentTab>
           <FluentTab Header="Second">…</FluentTab>
       </FluentTabStrip>

   Optional two-way <c>ActiveTabId</c> pass-through (round notification-templates-b3b): the chrome
   stays FluentUI's, and a caller that must KNOW which tab is active (the template editor loads the
   selected slot) binds it exactly as it would on <FluentTabs>. Omitted, the strip behaves as before. *@
<div class="fluent-tab-strip">
    <FluentTabs ActiveTabId="@ActiveTabId" ActiveTabIdChanged="@ActiveTabIdChanged">
        @ChildContent
    </FluentTabs>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The tab set — <c>FluentTab</c> elements, rendered through the chrome untouched.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// The id of the active <c>FluentTab</c> (its <c>Id</c>), forwarded to <c>FluentTabs</c>. Set it
    /// with <c>@bind-ActiveTabId</c> when the caller's state depends on which tab is showing;
    /// leaving it null keeps FluentUI's own first-tab default.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? ActiveTabId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Two-way binder for <see cref="ActiveTabId"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<string?> ActiveTabIdChanged { get; set; }
}